{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#define LL long long\nusing namespace std;\n//tim so chu so cua n\nint num(LL n){\n   int num = 0;\n    while(n){\n        n /= 10;\n        num++;\n    }\n    return num; \n}\n//tinh so co dang 11...1 lon nhat nhung khong vuot qua n\nLL find(LL n){\n    int ex = num(n);\n    LL cur = 0, ad = 1;\n    for(int i = 0; i <= ex-1; i++){\n            cur += ad;\n            ad *= 10;\n    }\n    if(cur <= n) return cur;\n    return ((cur-1)/10);\n}\n\nLL process(LL n){         \n    if(n <= 6) return n;\n    if(n <= 11) return (13 - n);\n    LL less = find(n);\n    LL more = less*10+1;\n    if(n % less == 0){\n        if(n <= more/2 + less) return num(less)*n / less;\n        return num(more) + process(more - n);\n    }\n    else{\n        LL _m = (n / less)*less;\n        LL res = process(_m) + process(n - _m);\n        if(n > more/2) res = min(process(_m) + process(n - _m), num(more) + process(more-n));\n        return res;\n    }\n}\nint main(){\n    LL n;\n    cin>>n;\n    cout<<process(n)<<endl;  \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "openai/gpt-4.1-nano"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    // Helper method to count the number of digits in n\n    public static int num(long n) {\n        int count = 0;\n        while (n != 0) {\n            n /= 10;\n            count++;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    // Find the largest number consisting of all '1's that does not exceed n\n    public static long find(long n) {\n        int ex = num(n);\n        long cur = 0, ad = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= ex - 1; i++) {\n            cur += ad;\n            ad *= 10;\n        }\n        if (cur <= n) {\n            return cur;\n        }\n        return (cur - 1) / 10;\n    }\n\n    public static long process(long n) {\n        if (n <= 6) {\n            return n;\n        }\n        if (n <= 11) {\n            return 13 - n;\n        }\n        long less = find(n);\n        long more = less * 10 + 1;\n        if (n % less == 0) {\n            if (n <= more / 2 + less) {\n                return num(less) * n / less;\n            }\n            return num(more) + process(more - n);\n        } else {\n            long _m = (n / less) * less;\n            long res = process(_m) + process(n - _m);\n            if (n > more / 2) {\n                long resAlt = process(_m) + process(n - _m);\n                long resOther = num(more) + process(more - n);\n                res = Math.min(res, resOther);\n            }\n            return res;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n        System.out.println(process(n));\n        scanner.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>0.95</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0018634299049153924, -1.9361264946837764e-07, -0.0001490716531407088, -0.017101440578699112, -0.000701707205735147, -5.490809417096898e-05, -3.128163257315464e-07,